## Report
Built the storage crate tests and wrote a focused integration test to exercise the error path. In `SharedStorageNode::create_multipart_upload`, the bucket write reservation is acquired (multipart_ops.rs:64-68) and multiple fallible `?` calls occur before the release at the end (multipart_ops.rs:69-89). The multipart uploads table enforces `owner_principal` length 1–256 (schema.rs:82-88), so a long principal can trigger a DB error mid-function. The PoC test (crates/storage/tests/reservation_leak.rs:31-67) uses a 300‑byte principal to force `object_pg.create_multipart_upload` to fail and then checks `active_write_reservations`. Running `cargo test -p storage create_multipart_upload_error_leaks_reservation -- --nocapture` panics with `active_write_reservations after error: 1` and an assertion failure showing left=1 right=0, confirming the reservation leak (see test_output.txt).

